---
// About and legal, as a full screen in the menu's place: what Dreamports is, the rules, how rights holders
// reach the Dreamports team, privacy and credits.
import OwnGameSteps from './OwnGameSteps.astro';
import ViewBar from './ViewBar.astro';
import { MINIMUM_AGE } from '../lib/players';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_NOTICES_URL, OWNER_URL, SOURCE_URL, SUGGEST_URL, pageTitle } from '../lib/site';

interface Props {
  // Open when the page loads, at /about/.
  open?: boolean;
}

const { open = false } = Astro.props;
const Title = open ? 'h1' : 'h2';
const Sec = open ? 'h2' : 'h3';
const sections = [
  { id: 'dreamport', label: 'What a Dreamport is' },
  { id: 'kinds', label: 'What you’ll find here' },
  { id: 'own-game', label: 'Bring your own game' },
  { id: 'legal', label: 'Not affiliated' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'For rights holders' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Your privacy' },
  { id: 'credits', label: 'Credits' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Get in touch' },
];
---

<dialog
  class="card view card-about"
  id="card-about"
  data-card="about"
  data-path="/about/"
  data-title={pageTitle('About and legal')}
  aria-labelledby="about-title"
  open={open}
>
  <div class="about">
    <nav class="about-nav" aria-label="About and legal">
      <Title id="about-title">About and legal</Title>
      {
        sections.map((section, index) => (
          <a href={`#${section.id}`} data-sec={section.id} aria-current={index === 0 ? 'true' : undefined} autofocus={index === 0}>
            {section.label}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </nav>
    <div class="about-text prose" tabindex="0">
      <section id="dreamport">
        <Sec>What a Dreamport is</Sec>
        <p>dreamports.net is a home for enhanced fan ports of classic games, made by a fan, for fans.</p>
        <p>
          A Dreamport is the port fans always dreamed of: the game you remember, with the extras you wished it
          had. It starts from the game as you know it, then adds the things fans have asked for over the years.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="kinds">
        <Sec>What you’ll find here</Sec>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Dreamports.</strong> The ports made here, by <a href={OWNER_URL}>Nahuel Genchi</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mash-ups.</strong> Great ports made by other fans, and fan games that aren’t ports, like
            Kirby’s Dead Land. Dreamports links to other fans’ own pages and credits the people who made them.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="own-game">
        <Sec>Bring your own game</Sec>
        <p>
          Dreamports never hosts game files: no <abbr class="caps" title="read-only memory">ROMs</abbr>, no game
          data and nothing taken from a game. It only lists projects that ask you to use your own legal copy, and
          before every play or download link it asks you to confirm that you are.
        </p>
        <OwnGameSteps />
      </section>

      <section id="legal">
        <Sec>Not affiliated with any publisher</Sec>
        <p>
          Dreamports is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Sega,
          Nintendo or any other publisher. Game names and trademarks belong to their owners, and appear here only
          to say which game a project works with.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site’s own design never uses publishers’ logos, box art or characters. Pictures of games come only
          from the makers’ own recordings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <Sec>For rights holders</Sec>
        <p>
          If you hold the rights to a game and want something on Dreamports taken down, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Rights%20notice`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>,
          with “Rights notice” in the subject. Say which game and what you’d like removed, who you are or whom you act
          for, and how to reach you. You can also send a notice through <a href={GITHUB_NOTICES_URL}>GitHub</a>, where
          the source code lives.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every game here lives in a folder of its own, so the Dreamports team can take it off dreamports.net and out
          of the source code in one change, usually within one business day. The team answers every notice, and
          never makes the sender’s details public. <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/docs/RIGHTS.md`}>How a notice is handled</a> has
          the details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy">
        <Sec>Your privacy</Sec>
        <p>
          There are no ads and nothing follows you around the web. The site keeps a few small notes in your own
          browser: whether you switched on menu sounds, which look and motion you picked, and, until you close the
          tab, which games you’ve confirmed you own. Those notes never leave your device, and “Forget my choices” in
          Settings clears your menu choices at any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sonic Advance Dreamport, played here on dreamports.net, keeps its own notes in your browser: your settings,
          the emeralds and achievements you’ve collected and, unless you untick “Remember on this device”, your game
          files, so you don’t have to add them on every visit. They never leave your device, except your achievements
          while you’re signed in to a profile, and clearing this site’s data removes them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <a href="/profile/">profile</a> is up to you, for players aged {MINIMUM_AGE} or older. It keeps the name
          you pick, your achievements with the day you earned each one, and, for each account you sign in with
          (Google, Discord, Steam or GitHub), only the id that service gives it. Dreamports never gets that account’s
          email address, password, name or friends, and keeps no password of its own. While you’re signed in, one
          cookie keeps you signed in, and your browser notes your player name so the games know to send your
          achievements. Your profile is private unless you make it public;
          then anyone can see your name, the day you joined and your achievements, and nothing else. From your
          profile you can download everything it keeps, or delete it for good.
        </p>
        <p>
          To see which pages people read, the site counts visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>.
          It notes the page you opened, the site that sent you there, your browser, your country and how fast the
          page loaded. It stores nothing in your browser, doesn’t keep your IP address and doesn’t follow you to
          other sites.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="credits">
        <Sec>Credits</Sec>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The site.</strong> Made by <a href={OWNER_URL}>Nahuel Genchi</a>.
            Its <a href={SOURCE_URL}>source code</a> is free to reuse under the MIT License.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Type.</strong> Set in <a href="https://github.com/IdreesInc/Monocraft">Monocraft</a> by
            Idrees Hassan, under the <a href="/licenses/monocraft-OFL.txt">SIL Open Font License</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Icons.</strong> From <a href="https://github.com/halfmage/pixelarticons">Pixelarticons</a> by Gerrit
            Halfmann, under the <a href="/licenses/pixelarticons-MIT.txt">MIT License</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sign-in marks.</strong> The Google, Discord, Steam and GitHub marks belong to their companies.
            Discord’s, Steam’s and GitHub’s come from <a href="https://simpleicons.org/">Simple Icons</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The star.</strong> Drawn by Narik,
            from <a href="https://soulofkiran.itch.io/pixel-art-animated-star">Pixel Art Animated Star</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The menu’s sounds.</strong> Made for Dreamports, and played by your own browser.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <Sec>Suggest a port, report a problem or get in touch</Sec>
        <p>
          Open an <a href={SUGGEST_URL}>issue on GitHub</a>. It takes a free GitHub account, and you don’t need to
          be a developer to fill it in. Please never attach game files.
        </p>
        <p>
          For anything else, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Rights holders have <a href="#rights">their own section</a>,
          above.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ViewBar href="/" />
</dialog>
